@[export lean_io_eprintln]
private def eprintlnAux (s : String) : IO Unit :=
  eprintln s

/--
Returns the directory that the current executable is located in.
-/
def appDir : IO FilePath := do
  let p ← appPath
  let some p ← pure p.parent
    | throw <| IO.userError s!"IO.appDir: unexpected filename '{p}'"
  FS.realPath p

namespace FS

/--
Creates a directory at the specified path, creating all missing parents as directories.
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/Init/System/IO.lean:898:@[extern "lean_io_app_path"] opaque appPath : IO FilePath

codex
The preflight’s artifact checks pass before the build subprocess, but Lean’s launcher cannot resolve its own application path in this sandbox. I’ve isolated Lake’s configuration separately and am tracing the failing Lean path resolution rather than substituting or faking the build result. The earlier generator-recorded clean build remains only provenance evidence, not my rerun.
